# text = And it came to pass that I began to be old; and, having no seed, and knowing king Benjamin to be a just man before the Lord, wherefore, I shall deliver up these plates unto him, exhorting all men to come unto God, the Holy One of Israel, and believe in prophesying, and in revelations, and in the ministering of angels, and in the gift of speaking with tongues, and in the gift of interpreting languages, and in all things which are good; for there is nothing which is good save it comes from the Lord: and that which is evil cometh from the devil.
# sent_id = 40
# llm_note = Very long sentence. AICTP root "came"(3). Main predicate in ccomp of "pass": "I began to be old"(7-11). Then semicolon introduces "I shall deliver up"(36) as the main assertion. "having no seed" and "knowing king Benjamin to be a just man" are conjoined participial advcl of "deliver"(36). "exhorting all men to come...languages" is advcl (participial) of "deliver". The list "in prophesying, and in revelations...languages" are all conjoined obliques of "believe"(58). "for there is nothing which is good save it comes from the Lord" is a causal advcl. "and that which is evil cometh from the devil" is a further conj.
